keywords:
  - Golomb-Welch conjecture
  - Lee metric
  - perfect code
  - lattice tiling
  - group ring
  - Lean 4
abstract: >-
  We prove that there is no lattice tiling of Z^35 or of Z^805 by Lee balls of
  radius three. These were the only cases left open by Xiao and Zhou among the
  Lee balls of dimension at least three and radius at least two with fewer
  than 2^30 points, so the lattice Golomb-Welch conjecture holds for all of
  them. Both theorems are checked in the Lean 4 kernel.
